2. WHAT YOU MAY DO (no fee, no permission needed)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Subject to the conditions below, any person is granted a personal,
non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

  (a) USE — install and run Outlaw Server on as many of your own machines as
      you like, for personal, educational, or internal purposes.
  (b) HOST — operate servers and services on machines running Outlaw Server,
      including services offered to others and services you charge for (e.g. a
      game server with paid membership). Charging for YOUR service is fine —
      Section 4(b) only forbids selling the Work itself.
  (c) STUDY — read, compile, and inspect the source code.
  (d) MODIFY LOCALLY — change the Work on your own machines for your own use,
      and for the purpose of developing improvements to submit back (Section 3).
  (e) TEST — download, run, and evaluate pre-release / beta builds, and report
      results.
  (f) SUGGEST CHANGES — submit bug reports, feature requests, and patches /
      pull requests to the Author's official repository.

